[ti:Welcome Home, Son]
[ar:Radical Face]

[00:01.30] 
[00:32.32] Sleep, don't visit
[00:36.97] So I choke on sun
[00:40.28] And the days blur into one
[00:44.22] And the backs of my eyes
[00:46.78] On the things I've never done
[00:50.70] Sheets are swaying from an old clothesline
[00:58.30] Like a row of captured ghosts over old dead grass
[01:04.93] Is never much but we've made the most
[01:09.74] Welcome home (home, home)
[01:28.36] (Home, home)
[01:35.29] Ships are launching from my chest
[01:43.14] Some have names but most do not
[01:46.89] If you find one, please let me know what piece I've lost
[01:53.50] Heal the scars from off my back
[02:01.16] I don't need them anymore
[02:04.78] You can throw them out or keep them in your mason jars
[02:12.67] I've come home (home, home)
[02:31.66] (Home, home)
[02:41.25] 
[02:49.93] All my nightmares escaped my head
[02:56.20] Bar the door, please don't let them in
[03:02.21] You were never supposed to leave
[03:08.44] Now my head's splitting at the seams
[03:14.73] And I don't know if I can
[03:21.46] 
[03:40.82] Here, beneath my lungs
[03:47.36] I feel your thumbs press into my skin again
[04:02.15] 
